Let $D\subset\mathbb R^d$ be bounded, choose $R$ with $D\subset B(0,R)$, and let $T$ and $\tau_R$ be the respective <Brownian exit time>[exit times]. Then $T\leq\tau_R$. Since
$$
|B_t|^2-dt
$$
is a <martingale>, the <optional sampling theorem for a supermartingale> at $\tau_R\wedge n$ gives
$$
d\,\mathbb E_x(\tau_R\wedge n)
=\mathbb E_x|B_{\tau_R\wedge n}|^2-|x|^2
\leq R^2-|x|^2.
$$
<Monotone convergence theorem> now gives
$$
\mathbb E_xT\leq\mathbb E_x\tau_R
\leq\frac{R^2-|x|^2}{d}<\infty.
$$

Solved by gpt-5.6-sol high.

= b
{parent=5}
